1118	\begin{proof}[Proof of \Cref{lem:qld-4-13}]
1119	We construct the measurements $\hat{Q}^\line_f$
1120	out of the lines measurements $T^{\line_X, \line_Z}_{f_X, f_Z}$
1121	guaranteed by \Cref{lem:qld-xz-lines}. To do so we first show how
1122	to map any line-point pair $(\line, u)$ in the expanded space
1123	$\F_q^{2m+2}$ to two pairs  $(\line_X, u_X)$ and  $(\line_Z, u_Z)$ in $\F_q^m$. We will 
1124	define $\hat{Q}^\line$ in terms of $T^{\line_X, \line_Z}_{f_X, f_Z}$ and
1125	show that the resulting measurement is consistent with the combined
1126	points measurement $\hat{Q}^{x,z,\alpha, \beta}$ from \Cref{lem:qld-4-12}.
1127	
1128	To define $\hat{Q}^\line$ we make use of the distribution $D$ from \Cref{lem:qld-sublines}. Let $D_{|\line}$ denote the distribution derived from $D$ by conditioning on the first element being $\line$. Then for every line $\line$ in $\F_q^{2m+2}$ and function $f \in \deg_{(md+1)}(\line)$, define
1129	\[ \hat{Q}^\line_f = \E_{(\line_X, \line_Z) \sim D_{|\line}} \sum_{\substack{f_X \in \deg_{md}(\line_X), f_Z \in \deg_{md}(\line_Z):\\ f = \combine_{f_X, f_Z}}} T^{\line_X, \line_Z}_{f_X, f_Z}\;, \]
1130	where $\combine_{f_X, f_Z}$ is defined in~\eqref{eq:combine-lines}. Note that $\{\hat{Q}^\line_f\}$ forms a valid POVM for every choice of line $\line$, and moreover that $\combine_{f_X, f_Z}$ is well-defined for the lines $\line, \line_X, \line_Z$ because of Property 2 of \Cref{lem:qld-sublines}. 
1131	
1132	Observe that by Property~3 of \Cref{lem:qld-sublines}, whenever $\line$ is axis-parallel, $\line_X$ and $\line_Z$ are axis-parallel also. Thus, in this case, by \Cref{lem:qld-xz-lines} it holds that the outcomes $f_X$ and $f_Z$ both have degree $d$. By definition of $\combine_{f_X, f_Z}$ it holds that the outcome $f$ of $\{\hat{Q}^\line_f\}$ has degree $d$ as well.
